OL,3,GNEWSASchools 'explosive device' email a
OL,4,Ahoax, say police
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn email threatening that "an explosive
OL,7,Fdevice" is located within hundreds of
OL,8,Fschools in Northern Ireland is being
OL,9,Ftreated as a "hoax" by the Police
OL,10,FService of Northern Ireland (PSNI).
OL,12,FAssistant Chief Constable Ryan
OL,13,FHenderson said police take "incidents
OL,14,Fof this nature very seriously" however
OL,15,F"at this stage we consider risk to the
OL,16,Fpublic as low".
OL,18,FSome schools have closed after
OL,19,Freceiving the email, however others
OL,20,Fhave decided to stay open and are
OL,21,Ftaking advice from the PSNI.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,420,410,260,120,0,100
